title: The Berlin Opposition
subtitle: Ruth Fischer and Arkadi Maslow turn Berlin against the Zentrale.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 10 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and offensive_gone = 0 and left_split = 0 and e21_left_leads = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 7

= The Berlin Opposition

Berlin-Brandenburg is the biggest district in the party, and since the summer the Left has run it. Ruth Fischer is twenty-five, Viennese, and a brilliant speaker with a gift for contempt. Arkadi Maslow, born in Russia and educated in Germany, writes her theses. In the Berlin factory cells, where unemployment is rising, their attacks on the united front go down well.

- @co_opt: Give Fischer work in the Zentrale.
- @isolate: Build our own minority in Berlin.
- @summon: Ask Moscow to invite Maslow to Moscow.

@co_opt
subtitle: Berlin calms down, and Fischer gets a platform across the country.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {loyalty: 10});
RG.setRole('fischer', 'Head of the work among the unemployed');
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 10;
!}

Fischer is given charge of the party's work among the unemployed. She uses it to build a following in every district.

@isolate
subtitle: Every district meeting in Berlin becomes a battle.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('berlin', {loyalty: -10, militancy: -5});
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

The Zentrale sends its own organisers to Berlin and builds a minority of the district around them.

@summon
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Moscow solves German problems by inviting them to Moscow. Fischer will carry on alone.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2 and comrade_maslow = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if comrade_maslow != 1 : Maslow is not in Berlin to be summoned. ?][? if comrade_maslow = 1 : The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids asking Moscow to intervene. ?]
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e21_maslow_moscow = 1;
RG.exile('maslow', {news: 'Maslow summoned to Moscow, and kept there', priority: 2});
Q.independence -= 5;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 4);
!}

The Executive invites Maslow to Moscow to answer some questions about his conduct in 1919. He goes, and is kept there. Fischer is more bitter than before.
